=head2 Features and required handling

=item C<managed-commands>

feature; refuse; since 3.3a. Managed commands require an exact declared daemon release profile.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/0b355ae8114511e1ff6359272b164f1cdf718e80/cmd.c>

=item C<format-tilde>

feature; refuse; since 3.3a. Six ordered substitutions encode delimiters, backslashes and dollar signs.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/0b355ae8114511e1ff6359272b164f1cdf718e80/format.c>

=item C<format-argument-quote>

feature; fallback; since 3.7. q/a is introduced in 3.7; older profiles use the tested tilde codec.

Fallback: C<format-tilde>.



Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/81f88f8517c9fc5371b56cf117530c6b477c96ac/format.c>

=item C<format-output-vis>

defect; repair; exact releases 3.4, 3.5, 3.5a. Reverse one VIS output layer before decoding the tilde field.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/9ae69c3795ab5ef6b4d760f6398cd9281151f632/server-client.c>

=item C<layout-classic>

feature; refuse; since 3.3a. Classic layouts remain available for old layouts and unnegotiated control clients.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/0b355ae8114511e1ff6359272b164f1cdf718e80/layout-custom.c>

=item C<layout-json>

feature; refuse; since 3.8. JSON layouts include floating placements in the current profile.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/7f2a35ad3321f9ba57a1062ca73b1f3ff26aca53/layout-custom.c>

=item C<control-mode>

feature; refuse; since 3.3a. Control framing is available at the support floor.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/0b355ae8114511e1ff6359272b164f1cdf718e80/control.c>

=item C<control-new-layouts>

feature; refuse; since 3.8. Enable new-layouts explicitly before interpreting new control layouts.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/7f2a35ad3321f9ba57a1062ca73b1f3ff26aca53/server-client.c>

=item C<pane-floating>

feature; refuse; since 3.7. Floating panes and their coordinates are available starting in 3.7.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/81f88f8517c9fc5371b56cf117530c6b477c96ac/cmd-split-window.c>

=item C<pane-modal>

feature; refuse; since 3.8. Modal panes and modal-window fields require 3.8.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/7f2a35ad3321f9ba57a1062ca73b1f3ff26aca53/cmd-split-window.c>

=item C<buffer-full>

feature; fallback; since 3.6. Use save-buffer when buffer_full is unavailable.

Fallback: C<buffer-save>.



Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/0dac7fe434d029a4f0b819cba8eb7963df291990/format.c>

=item C<buffer-save>

feature; refuse; since 3.3a. Binary save-buffer capture is separate from FORMAT framing.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/0b355ae8114511e1ff6359272b164f1cdf718e80/cmd-save-buffer.c>

=item C<layout-mirrored-main>

feature; refuse; since 3.5. Mirrored main-horizontal and main-vertical layouts require 3.5.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/ac44566c9c7e3e94d23be6def4c7ae83472543f5/layout-set.c>

=item C<split-percent-defect>

defect; refuse; exact releases 3.4. split-window -p is broken in 3.4; use the explicit -l percentage form.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/9ae69c3795ab5ef6b4d760f6398cd9281151f632/cmd-split-window.c>

=item C<break-pane-name-defect>

defect; refuse; exact releases 3.7. tmux 3.7 ignores explicit break-pane names and dereferences a null name in the unnamed multi-pane path; refuse break-pane before dispatch.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/81f88f8517c9fc5371b56cf117530c6b477c96ac/cmd-break-pane.c>

=item C<name-separator-defect>

defect; refuse; exact releases 3.7. tmux 3.7 rejects colon and dot names; validate their capability before dispatch.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/81f88f8517c9fc5371b56cf117530c6b477c96ac/tmux.c>

=item C<session-name-separators>

feature; refuse; since 3.7a. Literal dot and colon in session names require 3.7a; earlier releases replace or reject them.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/0e418b62d259ce8da8970f75732cc6632ee4c3a0/tmux.c#L285>

=item C<window-name-separators>

feature; refuse; since 3.3a. Literal dot and colon in window names are supported unless the declared separator defect applies.



Blocked by: name-separator-defect.

Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/0b355ae8114511e1ff6359272b164f1cdf718e80/window.c#L405>

=item C<pane-empty-flag>

feature; refuse; since 3.7. Explicit empty split panes use -E from 3.7; older releases require the declared empty-argument adapter.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/81f88f8517c9fc5371b56cf117530c6b477c96ac/cmd-split-window.c>

=item C<window-empty>

feature; refuse; since 3.8. Empty window creation requires the new-window -E flag from 3.8.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/7f2a35ad3321f9ba57a1062ca73b1f3ff26aca53/cmd-new-window.c>

=item C<break-pane-single-print>

feature; refuse; since 3.6. Breaking the only pane prints its returned identity from 3.6; older releases need an explicit scoped identity acquisition.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/0dac7fe434d029a4f0b819cba8eb7963df291990/cmd-break-pane.c>

=item C<pane-floating-move>

feature; refuse; since 3.8. Floating pane position and stack changes require move-pane placement flags from 3.8.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/7f2a35ad3321f9ba57a1062ca73b1f3ff26aca53/cmd-join-pane.c>

=item C<control-job-output>

feature; refuse; since 3.5. Foreground run-shell job output is delivered to the command client from 3.5; earlier releases send it to pane view mode. This does not guarantee shell-output framing.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/ac44566c9c7e3e94d23be6def4c7ae83472543f5/cmd-run-shell.c>

=item C<menu-appearance>

feature; refuse; since 3.4. Menu border, style, selected style and initial choice flags are available from 3.4.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/9ae69c3795ab5ef6b4d760f6398cd9281151f632/cmd-display-menu.c>

=item C<menu-mouse>

feature; refuse; since 3.5. The display-menu -M flag enables mouse selection without a triggering mouse event from 3.5.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/ac44566c9c7e3e94d23be6def4c7ae83472543f5/cmd-display-menu.c>

=item C<popup-close-on-key>

feature; refuse; since 3.6. The display-popup -k flag requests close on any key from 3.6.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/0dac7fe434d029a4f0b819cba8eb7963df291990/cmd-display-menu.c>

=item C<popup-reset-flags>

feature; refuse; since 3.6. The display-popup -N flag resets existing popup flags from 3.6; omitted flags otherwise preserve the existing popup policy.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/0dac7fe434d029a4f0b819cba8eb7963df291990/cmd-display-menu.c>

=item C<prompt-literal-commas>

feature; refuse; since 3.6. The command-prompt -l flag retains commas in one prompt and initial input from 3.6.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/0dac7fe434d029a4f0b819cba8eb7963df291990/cmd-command-prompt.c>

=item C<key-binding-format>

feature; refuse; since 3.7. Key table, key, repeat, note and native command source can be projected with list-keys -F from 3.7.





Source: L<https://github.com/tmux/tmux/blob/81f88f8517c9fc5371b56cf117530c6b477c96ac/cmd-list-keys.c>

